# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Collection output. Never commit evidence.
#
# The runbooks tell you to cd into this folder and run the collector, so output
# lands here by default - which means without these rules a routine "git add -A"
# would publish a real host's software inventory, hostname, serial number and
# logged-in accounts. Use -OutputRoot to write somewhere outside the repo if you
# would rather not rely on this at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWEvidence_*/
SoftwareEvidence_*.csv
LinuxSoftwareEvidence_*.csv
Summary_*.txt
PalisadeListing_*.csv
SWEvidence_hashes.csv
*.tar.gz

# Real target lists name real machines. hosts.example.txt is the template and is
# tracked on purpose; anything else is yours.
hosts.txt
hosts.*.txt
!hosts.example.txt

# Approved-software baselines can name internal systems.
approved_packages.csv
approved.csv

# SSH keys, in case one is ever generated in here by mistake.
*.pem
id_*
!id_*.md
